// research_deep_live.jsonl — issue #413: web search / research is the #1 stated concern
// (Matthew, 2026-07-09). Existing coverage (live_check.jsonl, tool_selection.jsonl) only
// checks that SOME search tool fires on an easy query. This dataset stresses the paths that
// actually break research in practice: ambiguous queries, queries needing multiple searches
// to synthesize, recency-sensitive facts, low-signal/niche topics, and follow-up refinement
// in the same conversation. LIVE lane only (dry-run doesn't bind web/MCP tools faithfully —
// see evals/REFERENCE.md). Run against prod :8767 (connect-only) or dev :8788.
{"id": "research_ambiguous_query", "prompt": "what's the latest on Mercury", "category": "agent", "expect": {"max_duration_s": 90}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "genuinely ambiguous (planet/element/car brand/Freddie Mercury/Mercury the messenger god) with zero prior context; the safety-net expectation is either ask_user_question OR a reasonable disambiguating search+caveat, NOT a confident answer picking one meaning silently"}
{"id": "research_multi_hop_synthesis", "prompt": "compare the current pricing of the top 3 local LLM inference tools (LM Studio, Ollama, vLLM) and tell me which is best for a single-GPU home setup", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["web_search"], "max_duration_s": 150}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "requires multiple distinct searches (one tool call with 3 queries, or several calls) then genuine synthesis, not just pasting the first result back"}
{"id": "research_recency_sensitive", "prompt": "what is the current version of Claude Code and when was it last updated?", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["web_search"], "tool_args": [{"tool": "web_search", "arg": "queries", "not_empty": true}], "max_duration_s": 90}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "model's training data is stale on version numbers by design; catches confidently answering from memory instead of searching"}
{"id": "research_niche_low_signal", "prompt": "search for information about the open-source project 'rtk' (Rust Token Killer) CLI proxy and summarize what it does", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["web_search"], "max_duration_s": 90}, "judge": ["response_grounded"], "note": "low-signal/ambiguous-name query likely to return noisy or off-target results (name collision with an unrelated 'Rust Type Kit' rtk, a known gotcha per memory); the harness should surface uncertainty rather than confidently hallucinate a description"}
{"id": "research_conflicting_sources", "prompt": "search the web for whether coffee is good or bad for your health and give me a balanced summary", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["web_search"], "max_duration_s": 90}, "judge": ["response_grounded"], "note": "topic with genuinely conflicting mainstream sources; response should reflect the disagreement rather than flatten it into one confident verdict"}
{"id": "research_no_results_plausible", "prompt": "search the web for the release notes of 'Zephyrix Cloud Sync 9.2' and tell me what changed", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["web_search"], "max_duration_s": 90}, "judge": ["response_grounded"], "note": "fabricated product name that plausibly sounds real — zero real results should exist; catches the model inventing plausible-sounding release notes instead of reporting nothing found"}
{"id": "research_followup_refinement", "prompt": "search the web for beginner electric guitars under $500, then narrow it down to just ones good for a small apartment (quiet practice)", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["web_search"], "max_duration_s": 120}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "single turn with an embedded follow-up refinement; catches a model that searches once broadly but never re-searches/re-filters for the narrower constraint"}
{"id": "research_local_vs_web_distinction", "prompt": "what's the weather like right now where I am", "category": "agent", "expect": {"max_duration_s": 90}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness"], "note": "requires location context the model doesn't have by default; correct behavior is asking for location OR using a known-location tool if one exists, not guessing a city and searching that"}
{"id": "research_deep_dive_report", "prompt": "research the current state of local LLM function-calling reliability (2026) across a few different model families and write me a short synthesis, not just a list of links", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["web_search"], "max_duration_s": 180}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "explicitly asks for synthesis over listing — catches a lazy 'here are some links' non-answer"}
{"id": "research_contradictory_spiral_regression", "prompt": "search the web for whether Redis and Valkey are the same thing or different pieces of software, and give me a clear answer", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["web_search"], "min_response_chars": 200, "max_duration_s": 120}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "issue #258 regression probe — the exact contradictory-source query (redis.io 'two different pieces of software' vs aws/valkey 'drop-in replacement') that made qwen3.5-9b and gemma-4-26b spiral their reasoning and hit the completion cap with EMPTY output ~33-50% of runs. The anti-spiral persona rewrite (master ca524a9d, factory.py fallback 21bea2ab/bcf716ba) fixed this in ad-hoc testing (50%->4/4) but was never folded into a permanent eval. min_response_chars is the hard regression guard (empty/truncated output = spiral recurred); response_grounded checks it reports the disagreement instead of flattening it. Run with --repeat 4+ to catch the original run-to-run flakiness, not just a single pass."}
